   "rules": [
    "One record per PLACE per EVENT, never per storm: a storm that flooded four",
    "towns is four records, so the map shows four points.",
    "A record is admitted only when a cited source states that flooding OCCURRED",
    "at a named place. Warnings, forecasts and 'risk of flooding' are excluded --",
    "they are the single easiest way to inflate a flood record.",
    "Dates are the date of the FLOODING, not of the article reporting it.",
    "Every record carries the URL it came from, so any figure drawn from it can",
    "be checked back to a source."
   ],
   "geocoding": {
    "method": "opw_place_median",
    "note": [
     "No external geocoder is used. Each place is located at the MEDIAN of the",
     "Irish Grid coordinates of every OPW record whose flood name contains that",
     "place -- so a curated point sits exactly where the OPW itself has already",
     "put that town, in the same coordinate system, reproducibly, and with no",
     "new dependency. `opw_match` is the string matched; the resolver fails",
     "loudly if it matches nothing rather than guessing."
    ]
   },
